(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[14 1 "// Finalization (PYS9 (a); doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 218\"): pyi has no reference counts, so an object's"] [15 1 "// death is Go's collector's finding. A tracked object (one with weak references, or with a finalizer's work due: a"] [16 1 "// class's __del__, a generator's close, a socket's warning) has a Go finalizer and a record in tracked, keyed by its"] [17 1 "// address and never holding it. Go's finalizer goroutine only moves the dead object into finQueue and sets the eval"] [18 1 "// breaker's bit; the thread holding the GIL drains the queue (handleEvalBreaker, gc.collect). The order is reference"] [19 1 "// counting's (subtype_dealloc): the work first, the Go finalizer set again without it (PEP 442: once only); found"] [20 1 "// unreachable again, the weak references are cleared (in the Go finalizer, under finMu, so no weak reference yields"] [21 1 "// the object after it) and their callbacks called in CPython's list order. Go's heap does not move and an object with"] [22 1 "// a finalizer is kept until the finalizer ran, so a weak reference's hidden address is valid while it is not cleared."] [24 1 "// the work a tracked object's death runs"] [26 23 "// its class's __del__ (slot_tp_finalize)"] [27 23 "// a generator's, coroutine's or async generator's finalization (_PyGen_Finalize)"] [28 23 "// an open socket's ResourceWarning and close (sock_finalize)"] [31 1 "// finTrack is a tracked object's record."] [33 21 "// the object's pointer's element type, to rebuild it from its address"] [34 21 "// its weak references in CPython's order: the basic ref, the basic proxy, then the newest first"] [35 21 "// the work due at its death"] [36 21 "// its identity once hashed (identityHash; an instance keeps it in its own field)"] [39 1 "// finItem is a dead object's turn in the queue: obj and its work, or (obj nil) its weak references' callbacks."] [46 24 "// tracked, finQueue, the weak references' addresses (Go's finalizer goroutine takes it too)"] [49 26 "// the Go finalizers run so far (gc.collect waits until it stays still)"] [50 26 "// a drain is running (under the GIL): a nested one leaves the queue to it"] [52 18 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: nothing tracked (the weak references hold their referents, as before 218)"] [57 1 "// addrOf is o's address (o a pointer: finTrackable)."] [60 1 "// hiddenPtr reads the address *u as a pointer (a weak reference's referent, alive while not cleared)."] [63 1 "// toObject is the object of type *elem at the address *u (a weak reference's referent; finMu held, *u not 0)."] [68 1 "// finTrackable is o's possible tracking: a pointer to a non-empty type of this package (another package's objects"] [69 1 "// may have their own Go finalizer, which a second SetFinalizer would abort on: _bz2's, _sqlite3's, _zstd's)."] [78 1 "// trackLocked is o's record, made (with its Go finalizer) when o has none; finMu held."] [93 1 "// trackWork tracks o (finTrackable) with the work w due at its death."] [104 1 "// goFinalized is the Go finalizer of every tracked object, run on Go's finalizer goroutine: o into the queue."] [130 1 "// drainFinalizers runs the queue under the GIL until it is empty: the number of dead objects handled."] [175 2 "// the record stays (its Go finalizer set again) while weak references, new work or an identity need it"] [188 1 "// weakCallbacks calls the callbacks of a dead object's weak references, in its list's order (PyObject_ClearWeakRefs)."] [202 1 "// runDel is slot_tp_finalize: the class's __del__ called, its exception to sys.unraisablehook."] [213 1 "// finalizeGen is _PyGen_Finalize: an async generator with sys's finalizer hook handed to it; a coroutine never"] [214 1 "// started warns; a suspended generator or coroutine closed."] [234 1 "// warnUnawaitedCoroutine is _PyErr_WarnUnawaitedCoroutine: warnings._warn_unawaited_coroutine(coro), or a plain"] [235 1 "// RuntimeWarning when that failed other than by the warning itself."] [256 1 "// finUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable from a finalizer (the object None)."] [263 1 "// finRound is one round of gc.collect: Go's collection, a wait until Go's finalizer goroutine has been still for a"] [264 1 "// moment (there is no public barrier), then the drain; the number of dead objects handled."] [281 1 "// finCollect is gc.collect's finalization: rounds until one handles nothing (at most 8), none when nothing is"] [282 1 "// tracked or queued; the number of dead objects handled."] [285 2 "// the classes' attribute caches out of date are dropped now, not at their next lookup: a stale answer (a method"] [286 2 "// deleted from its class) would keep its value alive"] [309 1 "// finalizeSocket is sock_finalize: an open socket warns ResourceWarning \"unclosed %R\" (its source the socket), then"] [310 1 "// its descriptor is closed."] [327 1 "// resourceWarn is PyErr_ResourceWarning(source, 1, msg): warnings.warn(msg, ResourceWarning, 1, source=source)."] [341 1 "// growStack gives f's value stack room for n more values in a new array, the old one's values cleared: newFrame's one"] [342 1 "// allocation holds the fast locals and the stack's first array together, so the stack's stale values there would keep"] [343 1 "// their objects reachable through the fast locals for the frame's life (queue 218: found by a weak reference that a"] [344 1 "// function's first call did not clear)."] [353 1 "// pendingGens are the coroutines made, and the generators suspended in a try region, since the last flush (under the"] [354 1 "// GIL): one still not finished when the list is flushed (every 256, and in gc.collect) is tracked for its finalization,"] [355 1 "// so the common cases, a coroutine awaited at once and a generator run to its end, pay no Go finalizer (queue 218:"] [356 1 "// measured with bin/pyi aot, a coroutine 0.13 us untracked against 0.6 us tracked at creation; a generator with a"] [357 1 "// try 0.66 us against 1.0-1.2 us tracked at its first suspension)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[80 21] [84 27] [108 21] [168 29] [196 51] [208 42] [220 51] [229 24] [238 39] [239 64] [250 92] [258 25] [269 28] [269 55] [271 28] [293 16] [293 27] [316 51] [321 16]]} (go/file "finalize.go" :imports [


